  "raw": {
    "https://www.crandallu.ca/crandallwp20/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Ad_Psychology_Aug-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "FACULTY POSITION IN UNDERGRADUDATE PSYCHOLOGY",
      "description": " \n \n \n \nFACULTY POSITION IN UNDERGRADUDATE PSYCHOLOGY \n \nAcademic Rank:  A full-time tenure-track position as an Assistant Professor or higher if \nexperience and qualifications warrant. \n \nSalary & Benefits:  Based on education and experience as per the Crandall University Faculty \nHandbook. (Approximate range $68,590 - $90,480).  Includes a generous \nbenefit and retirement package.  \n \nApplication Deadline:  Applications will continuously be reviewed until the position is filled. \n \nStarting Date:  July 1, 2027  \n \nQualifications:  A doctorate in Psychology is required.  \n \nParticulars of the Position:  To be considered for appointment candidates must be committed to  teaching \nand pursuing scholarship from a Christian perspective and to the mission and \nthe statement of faith of the university (which can be found on our website: \nwww.crandallu.ca).   \n \nThe successful candidate for this position will need to teach a variety of \ncourses from introductory to senior level within his/her range of expertise.   \n \nTeaching Load:  Six semester courses per year or equivalent. \n \nOther Duties:  In addition to teaching, research and service are obligatory components of this \ntenure-track position.  The successful candidate will serve as academic advisor \nto students enrolled in the undergraduate psychology program and will be \nexpected to function on at least one university committee annually. In \naddition, Faculty are encouraged to be involved within their respective \ndiscipline’s professional organizations or agencies. They are also encouraged \nto find their role of service within a local church and their community.    \n \nIn accordance with Canadian immigration regulations, this advertisement is addressed first to Canadian \ncitizens and permanent residents. \n \nCrandall University is a growing Christian university offering baccalaureate degrees in Arts, Business  \nAdministration, Science, and Education and master ’s degrees in Education and Management. Located in \nMoncton, New Brunswick, Canada, it was established by, and is sponsored by, the Canadian Baptists of Atlantic \nCanada. Crandall University is provincially chartered to grant degrees and certificates for undergraduate and \ngraduate programs and serves students from across Canada and around the world. \n \nQualified candidates should submit a letter of application, CV, evidence of teaching quality (teaching \nportfolio), research statement, a one-to-two-page statement describing their Christian faith commitment and \nhow it shapes their academic work, and the names of and contact information for three references to: \n \nProvost & Vice President for Academic Affairs \ncareers@crandallu.ca \nPlease use the following in the subject line of the email: \n \nRef: CU202608001Application for Psychology Position \n \nWe thank all applicants for their interest, but only those selected for an interview will be contacted. \n \n"
    },
    "https://www.crandallu.ca/crandallwp20/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Job-Posting-Custodian-and-Conference-Support-Worker-September-2026.pdf": {
      "title": "The Custodian and Conference Support Worker will report to the Maintenance Coordinator in the daily operations",
      "description": " \n \n \nCRANDALL UNIVERSITY | PO BOX 6004 | MONCTON | NEW BRUNSWICK | CANADA | E1C 9L7 \nCRANDALLU.CA \n \n \nCUSTODIAN AND CONFERENCE SUPPORT WORKER \n \n \nDepartment: Facilities Management \nContract:  Full Time \nEffective: October 1, 2026 (TBD) \n \n \nJob Summary: \nThe Custodian and Conference Support Worker will report to the Maintenance Coordinator in the daily operations \nand maintenance tasks associated with Crandall University’s buildings, grounds, and facilities.  This person will \nperform custodial duties along with light maintenance duties, grounds keeping such as snow removal and \nlandscaping.  The position will also provide support to the Director of Auxiliary Services in setting up rooms and \nproviding custodial services during conferences and events. \n \nThis position is normally expected to work Tuesday -Saturday, 8:30 -4:30. Schedule may be adjusted to \naccommodate winter needs.  Overtime may be required on occasion. \n \nKey Duties: \n1. Act as custodian and perform the day-to-day care and maintenance of the grounds, buildings, and \nfurnishings. \n2. Perform snow and ice control duties, as required, including driving the tractor. \n3. Assist with the setup of rooms for events, including but not limited to, relocation of furnishings, as \nrequired. \n4. Perform custodial duties to support events. \n5. Assist with maintaining residence facilities during the primary conference season, as necessary. \n6. Assist with building security, as required. \n \n \nQualifications: \n• Minimum high school diploma. \n• At least one year of experience in janitorial/custodial field. \n• Must be able to work independently with minimal supervision. \n• Must be attentive to detail and possess the ability to follow oral and written instructions carefully. \n• Must be able to work within a team environment. \n• Must be able to work various shifts, as needs arise. \n• Must be able to meet the physical demands of walking or standing (over 80% of the time) in addition to \nbending, stooping, squatting, crawling, climbing and lifting heavy objects (50+ lbs).   \n• Must have a valid driver's license. \n• Must demonstrate a commitment to the mission of the University  of “transforming lives through quality \nuniversity education firmly rooted in the Christian faith”. \n \n \nThe Application Process: \nIn accordance with Canadian immigration regulations, this advertisement is addressed first to Canadian citizens \nand permanent residents. Crandall University is committed to excellence in its hiring practices, and will accept \ninternal and external applicants in seeking the most qualified candidate. \n \nCrandall University is a growing Christian university offering baccalaureate degrees in Arts, Business \nAdministration, Science, Organizational Management and Education and master degrees in Education and \nManagement. Located in Moncton, New Brunswick, Canad a, it was established by and is sponsored by the \nCanadian Baptists of Atlantic Canada. Crandall University is provincially chartered to grant degrees and certificates \nfor undergraduate and graduate programs and serves students from across Canada and around the world. \n \nCRANDALL UNIVERSITY | PO BOX 6004 | MONCTON | NEW BRUNSWICK | CANADA | E1C 9L7 \nCRANDALLU.CA \n \n \n \n \nTo be considered for appointment, candidates must demonstrate an understanding of and freely embrace the \nUniversity’s Mission Statement and Statement of Faith. Short listed candidates will receive copies of these two \ndocuments prior to the interview. \n \n \nSalary: Level 1 ($35,870 – $44,180); placement on scale based on experience \n \nApplication deadline:  September 18, 2026.  Competition will remain open until the position is filled. \n \nPlease forward resume and cover letter to: Hiring Manager \n careers@crandallu.ca \n \nPlease use the following in the subject line of the email: Ref: CU202608002 Application for the role of \nCustodian and Conference Support Worker \n \n \nWe thank all applicants for their interest, but please note that only those selected for an interview will be \ncontacted. "
    }
